there are SCSI driver problems and I don't see that getting any better
this year. There has been some discussion and efforts last month but
the process seems to have died. For now the machine will run OpenBSD
with both of the Symbios Logic controllers and dual ethernet and a even
a 4mm DAT tape drive. All of that has been tested by me.

I have not tried any Linux variant.

I will not look at NetBSD any further and perhaps some year the SCSI
driver issues may pop up again. Seems I am the only person affected by
this anyways.

So long and thanks for all the fish.


-- 
--
Dennis Clarke
RISC-V/SPARC/PPC/ARM/CISC
UNIX and Linux spoken



